{
  "version": "1.2.1",
  "changelog": "New in 1.2.1 \u2014 the door gets its hand. The 1.2.0 install carried the bootstrap launcher, but its built-in updater was still the old Help-menu checker, so a staged update could never be fetched. This release wires the real self-update in: the editor now checks the channel in the background when it opens, downloads and hash-verifies a newer version into your own updates folder, and runs it on the next launch \u2014 no reinstall, no admin password. It also switches reporting on: session summaries, timings for heavy operations (group deletes carry their piece count), and errors now go silently to the same Player Reports inbox as the game's, and a corrupted update download \u2014 refused, with the installed version running untouched \u2014 files an update-refused report instead of failing silently. Help -> Check for Updates now speaks the same language: an already-downloaded update says it runs next launch. No editing behaviour changes.",
